### `Apk build fails after a Flutter SDK bump`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `flutter build apk` dies on Gradle/AGP/Kotlin "lower than Flutter's minimum" | Each stable raises minimums for all three; they surface one per build, and each cold retry costs minutes | Read the `DependencyValidationException` line — it names the exact minimum. Bump Gradle wrapper + AGP (`settings.gradle.kts`) + Kotlin in one pass. Run `flutter build apk --debug -v > log` — non-verbose mode hides Gradle output entirely |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Async test fails on a fixed delay after a new pre-work phase is added`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Test that waits a fixed ms, then asserts on a row/file/cancel, flakes or fails after new HTTP calls were inserted before the phase it watches | Fixed delays race whatever async work precedes the observable state | Poll for the observable (row exists, file exists) with a bounded loop, then act. HTTP counting wrappers: exclude metadata endpoints sharing the byte-route path prefix (e.g. an availability probe under `/chunks/`) or new probes break old request counts |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Unhandled async error from a previous test fails the next test`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A passing test fails with a resource-closed error ("Can't re-open a database after closing") that the runner attributes to a later test | Background worker loop outlives its owner: teardown closes the DB while the worker still polls it; the unhandled error lands in whatever test runs next | `stop()` must await loop exit (completer wired to the loop's `whenComplete`) before teardown closes resources. Also make cancel-during-startup paths throw the cancel exception, not a generic "incomplete" error |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `iOS tests skipped because there is no Mac`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| iOS branch has no assertions | Runner cannot launch on this Linux host | Write the platform code and expected tests against a mock channel. Mark the cases that need a device as Mac-only. Do not delete the expected assertions. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Channel reply never arrives or debug build asserts`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Dart `await invokeMethod` hangs; debug logs show a threading violation | Method-channel handler dispatched the reply from a worker/pool thread — `MethodChannel.Result` must be touched on the platform main thread | Wrap every off-main `result.success/error` in a main-handler post. Heavy radio/socket work goes on the pool; only the reply hops back |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Binder callback never arrives`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Privileged call returns null after a multi-second wait, or the app ANRs | The wait was posted onto the main looper, and the callback that should release it is delivered there too | Wait on a worker. Post only the channel reply. Do not block the main thread on a binder or permission callback the main looper must run |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `EventChannel has no test harness`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Native-side streams are untested on Linux | Repo had zero EventChannel mocks | Use `TestDefaultBinaryMessengerBinding.instance.defaultBinaryMessenger.setMockStreamHandler(EventChannel(...), MockStreamHandler.inline(onListen: ...))`; the sink arg pushes events with `.success(...)`. Clear every handler in `tearDown` or tests bleed into each other |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Apk compiles, old devices crash at runtime`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `NoSuchMethodError` on a handset below a certain API level, build and analyze green | Kotlin compiles against compileSdk: `flutter analyze` runs no Android Lint, so post-minSdk calls are invisible to the gates | Guard every method newer than minSdk with `Build.VERSION.SDK_INT` — known traps: GATT/hotspot-era Wi-Fi APIs (`WifiNetworkSpecifier` 29+, 3-arg `requestNetwork` 28+), `WifiP2pManager.Channel.close()` 27+, `canUseFullScreenIntent` 29+, FSI settings intent 34+. Below the guard, reply the channel error code instead |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Presenting a closed window crashes`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A later present call uses a freed window instead of returning a missing-window channel error | The window pointer was stored with no destroy signal | Clear that pointer from the window's destroy handler before any later present |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Parked channel result is dropped`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `await invokeMethod` never returns after stop, or when the radio is already off | The native side stored the result and cleared it, or waited for a state callback that will not change | Invoke that result before clearing it. If the radio is already in a terminal failure, reply the error immediately |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Swift call copied from an Objective-C header does not compile`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| No member for a name that the header lists, or a class method "has been renamed" | An Objective-C method imports as a Swift call with parentheses. A Swift 3 rename in the SDK is the name that compiles | Read the SDK header, then typecheck the call. Use the rename the compiler prints |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Host-only health row missing on this machine`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `firstWhere` throws because a Linux-only health row is absent | The test reads `dart:io` `Platform` and this host is another OS | Return before the assertion when that OS is not the current one. Keep the assertion for the OS that adds the row |

